	// R| # nonparametric component of a model formula specified by a call to rqss().  A sparse form
	// R| # of the Frisch Newton algorithm is eventually called to compute the estimator.
	// R| # Optional monotonicity and/or convexity/concavity constraints can be specified.  If
	// R| # the formula consists of a single qss component then the estimator solves the
	// R| # following variational problem:
	// R| #
	// R| #       min sum rho_tau (y_i - g(x_i)) + lambda V(g')
	// R| #
	// R| # where V(f) denotes the total variation of the function f.  The solution is a piecewise
	// R| # linear function with "knots" at the observed x_i points.  Additive models can consist
	// R| # of several components of this form plus partial linear and triogram components.
	// R| # To resolve the identifiability problem we delete the first column of the qss design
	// R| # components.  On return F contains the fidelity portion of the design, A is the penalty
	// R| # contribution of the design, R the constraint portion, and r the rhs of the constraints.
	// R| #
	// R| # Constraints are specified by the constraint argument:
	// R| #
	// R| #	N	none
	// R| #	I	monotone increasing
